---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Game from '../components/Game';
---
<Layout>
  <Game client:load />
  <section class="how-section" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE PLOT IS SIMPLE</p><h2 id="how-title">Big film knowledge.<br/>Small, daily ritual.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/how-to-play/">Read the full script <span>↗</span></a></div>
    <div class="how-grid"><article><span class="step-no">01 /</span><h3>Read the scene.</h3><p>Seven prompts, the same for everyone. From familiar favorites to the director’s cut.</p></article><article><span class="step-no">02 /</span><h3>Go off script.</h3><p>Name one movie in 20 seconds. The less obvious your answer, the more points you earn.</p></article><article><span class="step-no">03 /</span><h3>Roll the credits.</h3><p>Discover the films you missed. Share a spoiler-free score and give a friend a run for it.</p></article></div>
  </section>
  <section class="ranks-section" aria-labelledby="rank-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">EVERY ANSWER HAS ITS MOMENT</p><h2 id="rank-title">From box office to deep cut.</h2></div><span class="muted">Seven scenes. A possible 700 points.</span></div><div class="ranks"><div><span>🍿</span><strong>Blockbuster</strong><b>+10</b><small>The crowd favorite.</small></div><div><span>🎟️</span><strong>Matinee</strong><b>+30</b><small>A familiar face.</small></div><div><span>🎞️</span><strong>Indie</strong><b>+60</b><small>A little offbeat.</small></div><div><span>📼</span><strong>Cult Classic</strong><b>+85</b><small>You know your films.</small></div><div class="rank-gold"><span>🏆</span><strong>One in a Reelillion</strong><b>+100</b><small>That’s your close-up.</small></div></div><p class="scoring-note">Early scores estimate popularity from Wikipedia views and Wikidata language coverage, then blend in eligible daily answers. Your score locks when you submit.</p></section>
  <section class="home-faq"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE THE LIGHTS GO DOWN</p><h2>A few good questions.</h2><p>Free to play. No account.<br/>Just you and your mental movie collection.</p></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>What is Reelillion?</summary><p>A daily movie trivia game with a twist: you supply a film that fits the prompt, and uncommon answers earn more points. It’s a three-minute celebration of everything you’ve watched.</p></details><details><summary>What if I spell a title wrong?</summary><p>We forgive small typos, punctuation and common aliases. If a title isn’t in our catalog, you can try again while the clock runs. A recognized movie that doesn’t fit locks in at zero.</p></details><details><summary>When is the next daily game?</summary><p>Seven new prompts arrive every day at midnight in New York (America/New_York), including daylight saving changes.</p></details><details><summary>Can I play with more time?</summary><p>Yes. Turn on Extra time before starting for 40 seconds per prompt. Your share card includes a timer so friends can compare fairly.</p></details><details><summary>Are the answers and popularity estimates exact?</summary><p>The catalog uses films with English Wikipedia entries. Rarity starts with Wikipedia views or Wikidata language coverage, so it is an estimate, not a count of players. Genre and film classifications follow Wikidata. We show observed choices separately when available.</p></details></div></section>
</Layout>
